1758:
{Let the air be cut. Let the quarter be opened. Let ground tremor come by that opening and by no other. | I that am within the ring call to thee that art without it. Approach the triangle and no farther. | By the seal I have cut, and by the blood still wet upon it: come.} {What becomes stone here stays stone, long after the battle is forgotten. | Stone holds its answer for an age and gives it all at once. | Weight is the working. Nothing about it is quick, and nothing about it yields.} {Come visibly, affably, and without delay, and in a shape that will not put out the lamp. | Strike as the hammer strikes, once, and let the once be sufficient. | Word upon word, and no breath taken between, for a breath is a door and I have shut every door.}

