1760:
{Hail, wind. Hail, water. Hail, thorn at the field's edge. I have come to claim what is owed. | I speak to the ground first, for the ground was here before every king and will bury them all. | Rain that has fallen, rain that falls, rain that will fall: I set my hand in all three.} {Something is pressed upon until it gives. | Everything is hurled, and the ground does the striking. | The air is already moving. The art is to seize its direction.} {Bramble to the flesh, nettle to the eye, and the thorn to the heart behind the ribs. | As the sap rises, rise. As the leaf falls, fall. As the year turns, turn. | I name the season it must be. The ground resists. I name it again, and the ground yields.}

{Ground, give me one season out of the seven thou holdest. One, and no more. | I set both hands on the ground and pour every intellect I own into it, and the ground drinks deep. | What was slow, be sudden. What was sudden, be slow. The year is one, and for this moment it is mine.} {Winter does not hate the leaf. It takes the leaf all the same. | The target only stands on the wrong side of a season that has been hurried. | Growth is the only force here, and growth is patient, and that is why it wins.}

{Cut the bramble back before dark, or it grows on in the direction it was pointed. | The ground remembers who asked. Ask wrongly once and walk that field a stranger all your days. | Leave an offering. What it is matters little. That it was left matters greatly.}

1769:
{Hail, wind. Hail, water. Hail, thorn at the field's edge. I have come to claim what is owed. | I speak to the ground first, for the ground was here before every king and will bury them all. | Hail to the elder at the ditch, that stood before the road was cut and will stand when it is dust.} {The working is a sentence passed, and the body serves it to the last hour. | A condition is laid on a body as a law is laid on a city, and the body keeps it. | Everything here changes the terms the foe must fight under.} {No pleading, no thanks. I say it plainly, as the hard winter says it. | What was slow, be sudden. What was sudden, be slow. The year is one, and for this moment it is mine. | By the first frost and the last, by the flood and its falling, by the hour the swallows leave.}

{Grow, grow, grow, and be swift, for I have asked and the asking is not refused. | Ice in the vein, blight in the leaf, and the long sleep after. | Let the cursed come as growth comes: without pity, without pause.} {The ground gives freely and remembers everything it gave. | Every charm is a loan against a season, and the season is repaid in full. | Winter does not hate the leaf. It takes the leaf all the same.}

{The last word is spoken low, and it is the true name of the field. | Burn the thorn that was used. Never leave a thorn lying with a name upon it. | Wash the hands in running water, downstream of where the working was done.}

1773:
{Every mind is a locked room. I am the one who was given the key, and then erased. | By the name struck from the record, and by the hand that struck it: attend. | PSI Hypnoshock. Spoken once. Indoors. By one voice. Never again by the same mouth.} {It goes by the readiest path and spares nothing standing on that path. | One instant, no warning, and afterward the smell no one needs to be taught. | The charge is the only part that is aimed. Everything after is conduction.} {I hold the certainty that one enemy is already beaten, and I hold it until it spreads. | Repeat the phrase eleven times. The true count is [REDACTED]. Eleven is enough to kill. | Attend to one enemy until one enemy gives way. Attention is the weapon, and it does not tire.}

{Do not blink at the wrong moment. There is a wrong moment, and it is watching. | Recite through the interruption. The interruption is not mine to fear. | I close every door in the head but one, and go out through the one that has no number.} {Range does not matter. A mind is never far from a mind. | The All is Mind. The rest of the sentence is above any mortal clearance. | The caster's psyche is spent as attention, and attention is the one coin that buys anything.}

