{Word, silence, word, silence, and in the silences the parts no hand could write. | I close every door in the head but one, and go out through the one that has no number. | I hold the certainty that one enemy is already beaten, and I hold it until it spreads.} {The wound is done by the target, to the target, on an order it never heard. | It works on anything with a mind, and the dark has always had one. | Mechanism: [REDACTED]. The words work. The why was buried with those who asked.}

{Open the eyes last. There is always something in the room that was not there before. | The room in {city} has no clock in it, and the one inside it still listens for a voice. | The quiet closes over the place like water, and nobody remembers having been crowded.}

972:
{Silence. Silence. [SIX WORDS WITHHELD]. Silence. | I call upon thee whose name was burned from the file and lives on behind my eyes. | Let the noise of the world fall away. What remains is [REDACTED], and it obeys.} {The battle is fought inside a mind, and the mind is not always the caster's. | Nothing here can be weighed. Will is the only blade. | The thought is aimed like a spear and driven through every wall of the skull.} {The mantra is only the fence the working walks along. | What is aimed at this company arrives as a thought first. Meet it there, while it is small. | I bind by clearance: whatever stands above my level, come down to it.}

{I narrow my psyche to a needle and I draw it through the dark. | I spend my psyche as a slow bleed, never a rush, until the world gives way first. | I pour the same steadiness into each of them and tell none of them where it came from.} {The ward is a shared conviction, and a conviction held by five is not five convictions. | Mechanism: [REDACTED]. The words work. The why was buried with those who asked. | Fear arrives before the blow. Meet the fear, and the blow arrives nowhere.}

{Take the conviction back before sleeping. Left in place it is dreamed, and dreams spread. | The closing words were removed. I say nothing, and I count to eleven, and it ends. | Psychoanalysis is ended. What it touched is not.}

976:
{Cleared for utterance. Say what is printed. What was struck out, say inwardly. | There is one thought in this room, and it is sharper than any blade in it. | Reaching is for hands. I attend, and distance kneels.} {The battle is fought inside a mind, and the mind is not always the caster's. | The whole of it is mass and speed, arriving together at the one point it was aimed. | Nothing here can be weighed. Will is the only blade.} {The mantra is only the fence the working walks along. | I close every door in the head but one, and go out through the one that has no number. | I hold the certainty that one enemy is already beaten, and I hold it until it spreads.}

{I put the kinetic into the thought and the thought into the head, and the head does the rest. | I whisper the one fear it was born with, and I whisper it louder. | I narrow my psyche to a needle and I draw it through the dark.} {It leaves the other no option of refusing. | The All is Mind. The rest of the sentence is above any mortal clearance. | The kinetic is real in the body, for the mind never learned to doubt the body's reports.}

{The room in {city} has no clock in it, and the one inside it still listens for a voice. | The quiet closes over the place like water, and nobody remembers having been crowded. | Its mind is a room with the lights put out. I took the switch with me.}
